WEBVTT

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:02.021
This article expands an

00:00:02.021 --> 00:00:03.481
11-slide interview deck into

00:00:03.481 --> 00:00:04.361
a technical reference

00:00:04.361 --> 00:00:05.461
on the Smart Fab Edge

00:00:05.461 --> 00:00:07.541
AI architecture. The appendix explains

00:00:07.541 --> 00:00:08.621
how to read the figures.

00:00:08.621 --> 00:00:10.450
It covers real-time processing,

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:13.001
anomaly detection, Remaining Useful

00:00:13.001 --> 00:00:14.941
Life (RUL) prediction,

00:00:14.941 --> 00:00:17.741
edge deployment, industrial knowledge retrieval,

00:00:17.741 --> 00:00:18.921
and AI agent boundaries.

00:00:18.921 --> 00:00:20.721
The real question is not

00:00:20.721 --> 00:00:21.681
how to deploy models,

00:00:21.681 --> 00:00:22.521
but how to run them

00:00:22.521 --> 00:00:23.670
under constrained resources —

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:26.821
balancing latency, compute, reliability,

00:00:26.821 --> 00:00:28.390
and operating cost —

00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:30.550
while integrating with existing controls,

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:33.277
maintenance workflows, and factory systems.
